after 15 and 40 days at 40°C. Sadler’s D value of 3.92 x 10-14 square centimeters (cm2)/second 
(s) for toluene at 40°C, which has been well characterized, was used in the model (Sadler et',17,'Appendix 1. Model of the Sorption of Surrogate Contaminants into Plastic','regulation','US','2021-07-01','public_domain','["PET"]','["rigid bottle"]');
