M14 
Remainder/ 
Composite Metal 
Remainder/ Composite Metal 
means metal that cannot be 
put in any other type. This 
type includes items made 
mostly of metal but combined 
with other materials and items 
made of both ferrous metal 
and non-ferrous metals 
combined. Includes products 
whose weight is derived 
significantly from the metal 
portion of its construction. 
Includes food-contaminated 
metals. Includes metal 
fragments smaller than two 
inches if easily identifiable as 
metal. 
Examples include metal 
appliances, motors, insulated 
wire, food-soiled metals (such 
as cookware, cans, and 
aluminum foil) 
