Roll Carts 
The RMA requires CAA to cover any cost differential when roll carts containing at least 10% post-consumer recycled 
(PCR) content cost more than comparable carts made from virgin material. To assess potential cost differences, CAA 
conducts quarterly market reviews by collecting pricing data from national suppliers for both virgin and PCR content 
roll carts. Pricing is analyzed by cart size to determine any material cost variance. Based on supplier pricing data for 
Q3 and Q4 2025, CAA found no material cost difference between virgin roll carts and those containing at least 10% 
PCR content. 
Finance Reconciliation 
The below table reflects the payments to Oregon jurisdictions for 2025 invoices at the time of Annual Report 
Submission (“2025 Invoices to Date”) and compares them to CAA’s internal Financial reporting and expense recognition 
for 2025 (“2025 Recognized Expenses (SOA)”). The SOA is CAA’s Schedule of Activity totals for the 2025 Fiscal Year.
